(6856999, 1032100, 108982, '<td valign="top">Great "life as it is" capture.  I personally have a love of this type of photography.  Absolutely dig the communication circuit...the girl holding phone, listening to mom while girl on the phone chats with another while doing her sister''s(?) hair and the little one''s look of subtle, incredulity is priceless! 10</td>', 'Great "life as it is" capture.  I personally have a love of this type of photography.  Absolutely dig the communication circuit...the girl holding phone, listening to mom while girl on the phone chats with another while doing her sister''s(?) hair and the little one''s look of subtle, incredulity is priceless! 10', '2012-09-05 14:30:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6857006, 1031651, 144365, '<td valign="top">#3, tied with another.<br/>Completely random for this challenge. When you see nothing but portraits and landscapes, anything which is different elicits a higher score over here. This one has the WTF element to it which brings it way up. I imagine there were many outtakes I would have ranked as high also.</td>', '#3, tied with another.Completely random for this challenge. When you see nothing but portraits and landscapes, anything which is different elicits a higher score over here. This one has the WTF element to it which brings it way up. I imagine there were many outtakes I would have ranked as high also.', '2012-09-05 14:32:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6857007, 1032029, 108982, '<td valign="top">when i opened this the screen was blank...???  Then I scrolled down to drop a big fat ZERO on it...well, a one anyway.  Then the boat appeared.  I am generally not a fan of MASSIVE negative space captures but this is an exception in my book.  Love, love, love this photo.  Never had one instantly jump from a 1 to 10...there is a first for everything.  Nice Job.</td>', 'when i opened this the screen was blank...???  Then I scrolled down to drop a big fat ZERO on it...well, a one anyway.  Then the boat appeared.  I am generally not a fan of MASSIVE negative space captures but this is an exception in my book.  Love, love, love this photo.  Never had one instantly jump from a 1 to 10...there is a first for everything.  Nice Job.', '2012-09-05 14:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
