(6860152, 1030042, 108580, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by HarveyG:</b></div><hr/><i> And who was (were) the chop who questioned the validity of this?<br/>This is easily done with off camera and flash and timed exposure.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Harvey, I''ve never heard the word "chop" used thay way, but assuming it''s an insult, well, back atcha.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You know what the say about assumption, it makes an ASS out of U and ME.<br/> <br/>Locally the word chop or in it''s native "Tjop" is more a term of endearment, almost like "silly nit". That''s the problem with type, it has no tone of voice. In Australia the word or phrase "you silly/stupid bastard" is perhaps a bit stronger and could possibly be used in a derogatory way but often in a way that borders on affection or awe! would you believe. And yes, I grew up in Australia but dare not use that phrase in Africa for fear of getting walloped. So chop it was :P There are far better words in Afrikaans that could be used to be insulting, trust me.<br/> <br/>Well done for fessing up. That''s pretty unheard of. You have a right to naturally, there is a mechanism for all of us to do so and Allesandro took offence at the time. SC can''t possibly have eyes everywhere.<br/> <br/>Lesson learnt, schools out :)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: Originally posted by HarveyG: And who was (were) the chop who questioned the validity of this?This is easily done with off camera and flash and timed exposure.  Harvey, I''ve never heard the word "chop" used thay way, but assuming it''s an insult, well, back atcha.  You know what the say about assumption, it makes an ASS out of U and ME. Locally the word chop or in it''s native "Tjop" is more a term of endearment, almost like "silly nit". That''s the problem with type, it has no tone of voice. In Australia the word or phrase "you silly/stupid bastard" is perhaps a bit stronger and could possibly be used in a derogatory way but often in a way that borders on affection or awe! would you believe. And yes, I grew up in Australia but dare not use that phrase in Africa for fear of getting walloped. So chop it was :P There are far better words in Afrikaans that could be used to be insulting, trust me. Well done for fessing up. That''s pretty unheard of. You have a right to naturally, there is a mechanism for all of us to do so and Allesandro took offence at the time. SC can''t possibly have eyes everywhere. Lesson learnt, schools out :)', '2012-09-08 14:57:08.000000', NULL, 0),
