(6860433, 1031810, 86218, '<td valign="top">Congrats Harvey on a 7+ score. Great shot and just missing out on a ribbon but at the rate you are now going in the FS..it will be comming soon I know. HM a great honour still and well...1x? whats that? Their loss :)</td>', 'Congrats Harvey on a 7+ score. Great shot and just missing out on a ribbon but at the rate you are now going in the FS..it will be comming soon I know. HM a great honour still and well...1x? whats that? Their loss :)', '2012-09-09 08:09:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860439, 1031710, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good catch, I like the dynamics here.</td>', 'Good catch, I like the dynamics here.', '2012-09-09 09:41:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860452, 1031943, 67152, '<td valign="top">I really like it the way it is right now.  I gave it a 7 during voting - absolutely loving the birds.<br/> <br/>I can see where <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=138630" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">nam</a> is going and upping the contrast to expand the tonal range, but I like the richness of the grays throughout.  I actually tried it, and had I been able to ''see this shot'', I would have like entered a much more pimped up and contrast-y version.</td>', 'I really like it the way it is right now.  I gave it a 7 during voting - absolutely loving the birds. I can see where  nam is going and upping the contrast to expand the tonal range, but I like the richness of the grays throughout.  I actually tried it, and had I been able to ''see this shot'', I would have like entered a much more pimped up and contrast-y version.', '2012-09-09 12:08:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860458, 1031821, 18197, '<td valign="top">@Ozzie, @Pelican and @Mita -<br/> <br/>The angles and tilts of the buildings are real. In Amsterdam, many of the buildings tilt toward the street so a rope and pulley system can hoist furniture to upper floors when moving in and out. The combination of these angles creates some pretty strange architecture. But i like it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-09-09 11:55:41.</i></td>', '@Ozzie, @Pelican and @Mita - The angles and tilts of the buildings are real. In Amsterdam, many of the buildings tilt toward the street so a rope and pulley system can hoist furniture to upper floors when moving in and out. The combination of these angles creates some pretty strange architecture. But i like it.', '2012-09-09 12:55:03.000000', '2012-09-09 12:55:41.000000', 0),
(6860460, 1031821, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> And another great ''Dutch'' scenery. I really love the processing. It reminds me of the images of Anton Pieck. Beautiful. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the kind words and I''m honored to be compared with Anton Pieck.</td>', 'Originally posted by Kroburg: And another great ''Dutch'' scenery. I really love the processing. It reminds me of the images of Anton Pieck. Beautiful.   Thanks for the kind words and I''m honored to be compared with Anton Pieck.', '2012-09-09 12:56:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860474, 1031477, 58785, '<td valign="top">Superb... again a 1 vote for a wonderful photo... must be an error!<br/>Congrats :)</td>', 'Superb... again a 1 vote for a wonderful photo... must be an error!Congrats :)', '2012-09-09 13:37:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860477, 1032079, 66384, '<td valign="top">Interesting that one commenter said the photograph is interesting, yet she it a 1. Odd way to vote. <br/> <br/>I like the shot a lot: terrific lighting, dramatic color and contrast, and the added interest of the photographer''s face in the background. I think it would be even stronger with a bit cropped off the bottom to bring the edge right up to the bottom of the podium.</td>', 'Interesting that one commenter said the photograph is interesting, yet she it a 1. Odd way to vote.  I like the shot a lot: terrific lighting, dramatic color and contrast, and the added interest of the photographer''s face in the background. I think it would be even stronger with a bit cropped off the bottom to bring the edge right up to the bottom of the podium.', '2012-09-09 13:49:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6860491, 1029433, 12253, '<td valign="top">Beautiful...congrat''s Mary!<br/></td>', 'Beautiful...congrat''s Mary!', '2012-09-09 15:10:50.000000', NULL, 0),
